WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.719
King Joffrey has FINALLY got his comeuppance.

00:00:02.719 --> 00:00:04.120
But WHO did it?

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:08.189
Let's look at who was in a position to OFF
Joff!

00:00:08.189 --> 00:00:13.379
Hey fellow Game of Thrones fans, it's JAN
here for Flicks And The City.

00:00:13.379 --> 00:00:16.930
What is it about Game of Thrones and whacking
people at weddings?

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:20.350
First, the Starks got it in the neck in season
3's RED Wedding.

00:00:20.350 --> 00:00:24.090
And then Joffrey got all choked up in season
4's PURPLE Wedding.

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:30.070
Ok, so no one died at Tyrion and Sansa's wedding,
but it wasn't EXACTLY a barrel of laughs now,

00:00:30.070 --> 00:00:31.070
was it?

00:00:31.070 --> 00:00:34.879
And don't forget Jaime Lannister's gentle
reminder to Loras Tyrell that if Loras ACTUALLY

00:00:34.879 --> 00:00:38.410
married Cersei she'd murder the Knight of
Flowers in his sleep!

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:41.630
Anyone would think George RR Martin had something
against marriage!

00:00:41.630 --> 00:00:46.340
Anyway, the BIG question the Purple Wedding
left us with was: Who Killed Joffrey?

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:51.149
One of TV's biggest whodunits since The Simpsons'
Who Shot Mr Burns?

00:00:51.149 --> 00:00:53.149
or Dallas's Who Shot JR?!

00:00:53.149 --> 00:00:55.089
So, just who are Westeros's Most Wanted?

00:00:55.089 --> 00:00:56.749
Well, for once, it's just about everyone apart
from Cersei!

00:00:56.749 --> 00:00:57.749
Let's look at the suspects.

00:00:57.749 --> 00:01:02.250
YES, Tyrion has been accused of killing his
nephew by Cersei, who says Joffrey pointed

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:03.399
at his uncle as he died.

00:01:03.399 --> 00:01:07.800
And YES, he does have PLENTY of reasons to
LOATHE Joffrey – not LEAST the relentless

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:11.820
humiliation he suffered during the wedding
festivities, including the sick spectacle

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:13.460
of the War of the 5 Kings.

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:18.120
And YES, he did have PLENTY of opportunity
as the King's Cupbearer at the wedding.

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:22.840
And Sansa DOES flee the scene of the crime,
MAYBE because she knew what her husband had

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:27.590
done, or MAYBE because Tyrion had arranged
for her to get out of harm's way in case he

00:01:27.590 --> 00:01:28.590
was caught.

00:01:28.590 --> 00:01:33.700
BUT, we all know that Tyrion has an unfortunate
history of being accused of crimes he didn't

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:34.700
commit!

00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:37.310
Remember Catelyn accusing him of pushing Bran
out of the tower?

00:01:37.310 --> 00:01:42.540
And LYSA accusing him of murdering her husband
Jon ARRYN, the King's Hand prior to Ned Stark?

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:47.500
Ok, so he DID tell his squire Podrick to pay
the dwarf entertainers after the wedding,

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:50.780
adding that ‘We'll have to find another
way to thank the King.'

00:01:50.780 --> 00:01:55.520
But although Tyrion is small in stature, he's
big in brain, which means he'd be WAY too

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:58.320
clever to put himself so obviously in the
firing line.

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:02.760
Had he ACTUALLY done the deed, I don't think
he'd be standing round picking up the incriminating

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:04.450
goblet after the event.

00:02:04.450 --> 00:02:09.249
But with mother of madness Cersei on his case,
let's just say he's gonna need a good lawyer

00:02:09.249 --> 00:02:13.999
or alternately, someone a bit skilful in a
skirmish to fight for him in a trial-by-combat

00:02:13.999 --> 00:02:18.599
situation just like Bronn did at the Eyrie.

00:02:18.599 --> 00:02:20.890
And so to the bride.

00:02:20.890 --> 00:02:23.459
Margaery Tyrell CERTAINLY knows her way around
the POLITICS of POWER.

00:02:23.459 --> 00:02:27.939
She married Renly Baratheon, DESPITE knowing
he was the LOVER of her brother Loras.

00:02:27.939 --> 00:02:32.209
She won over Joffrey with flattery when Loras
asked him to marry her in repayment for the

00:02:32.209 --> 00:02:34.799
Tyrells helping the Lannisters win Blackwater.

00:02:34.799 --> 00:02:39.889
And she's worn her "I-heart-Joffrey" T-shirt
well ever since then, with a little slip in

00:02:39.889 --> 00:02:44.250
episode 1 of season 4, when she commented
sarcastically to her grandmother Olenna that

00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:48.840
if Joffrey chose her wedding necklace it'd
PROBABLY be made of "DEAD SPARROW heads".

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:53.700
From both Margaery's own experience and Sansa's,
she was FULLY aware of the nature of the BEAST

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:54.999
she was marrying.

00:02:54.999 --> 00:02:59.529
Maybe she thought that if she WERE going to
throw herself WILLINGLY into the lions' den,

00:02:59.529 --> 00:03:03.650
it would be wise to make sure the one with
the most VICIOUS BITE was out of the way.

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:07.500
YES, she's been able to control Joffrey up
to THIS point, getting him to wave to his

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:09.569
people and give his leftovers to the poor.

00:03:09.569 --> 00:03:13.790
But how LONG would it be before he'd get BEYOND
her control, as happened to Cersei?

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:19.129
I mean, just look at Joffrey's sick re-enactment
of the War of the 5 Kings, and his treatment

00:03:19.129 --> 00:03:20.129
of Tyrion at the feast.

00:03:20.129 --> 00:03:22.349
Given both real-life AND Game of Thrones history,
with Joffrey dead, it's likely Margaery would

00:03:22.349 --> 00:03:25.150
wed his much-better-behaved brother Tommen.

00:03:25.150 --> 00:03:27.620
Game, set and match, Margaery, then.

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:30.579
Oh, and she certainly had her CHANCE to dispense
with the malicious monarch.

00:03:30.579 --> 00:03:35.560
After all, she was beside him throughout the
wedding festivities, handed him his gold goblet,

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:37.359
and even fed him his pie.

00:03:37.359 --> 00:03:42.989
AND she DIDN'T rush to his side to help him,
like Cersei did, as he lay dying on the floor.

00:03:42.989 --> 00:03:47.409
Also, was Joffrey pointing at Tyrion as he
died or was he ACTUALLY pointing at Margaery?!

00:03:47.409 --> 00:03:51.779
Plus, getting rid of Cersei's pride and joy
would doubtless give Margaery a bit of ADDED

00:03:51.779 --> 00:03:55.280
revenge on her mother-in-law for her Rains
of Castamere threat last season!

00:03:55.280 --> 00:03:56.280
So, Margaery's had TWO husbands now and BOTH
of them have died in mysterious circumstances.

00:03:56.280 --> 00:03:57.280
We know she wasn't behind Renly's death, of
course.

00:03:57.280 --> 00:03:58.280
Still, if I were the THIRD husband-to-be,
I wouldn't like THOSE odds!

00:03:58.280 --> 00:03:59.280
The Tyrells, however, ALWAYS seem to come
up smelling of roses

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:00.920
Could granddaddy Tywin have tired of Joffrey?

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:06.049
As terrifying as Tywin is, wouldn't Joffrey
only cower before him for so long?

00:04:06.049 --> 00:04:10.079
Could he REALLY have continued to order the
King to his chambers once he was a married

00:04:10.079 --> 00:04:11.079
man?

00:04:11.079 --> 00:04:14.780
Perhaps, Tywin thought it was time for a more
LIKEABLE Lannister to take the Iron Throne,

00:04:14.780 --> 00:04:17.470
and therefore make his life and position as
the Hand easier.

00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:20.250
But MOST IMPORTANTLY the new blood would be
PLIABLE.

00:04:20.250 --> 00:04:24.020
Step forward, Tommen, it's your turn!

00:04:24.020 --> 00:04:28.520
In fact, if you look CAREFULLY, you can see
Tywin protects Tommen from seeing Joffrey

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:29.520
die.

00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:31.259
And how would Tywin have done it?

00:04:31.259 --> 00:04:35.669
Well, the man's a master of machinations,
and it's not like he doesn't have EXPERIENCE

00:04:35.669 --> 00:04:37.830
with this sort of wedding, now, is it?

00:04:37.830 --> 00:04:41.770
Perhaps the new sword Tywin gifted Joffrey
for his wedding was actually laced with poison.

00:04:41.770 --> 00:04:45.710
So, when Joffrey used it to cut the wedding
pie, it poisoned the piece he ate.

00:04:45.710 --> 00:04:49.920
The dead dove we see in the pie was doubtless
caused by Joffrey striking it with his sword,

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:52.500
but it's still an interesting way to foreshadow
his death.

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:55.819
But wouldn't OTHERS have eaten the pie at
the feast and therefore been affected too?

00:04:55.819 --> 00:05:01.580
Well, yes, BUT we never actually SEE anyone
else eat the pie – though we DO see Olenna

00:05:01.580 --> 00:05:03.530
and Tywin with a forkful of something.

00:05:03.530 --> 00:05:08.389
But SURELY as King, Joffrey would be the FIRST
to scoff down his piece, and once you've seen

00:05:08.389 --> 00:05:13.100
the King drop dead after eating HIS pie, I'm
guessing that might put you off yours!

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:17.770
And remember, Joffrey's new sword, the Widow's
Wail, as he names it, was actually melted

00:05:17.770 --> 00:05:19.680
down from Ned Stark's sword Ice.

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:25.310
And wouldn't that be a delightful irony – the
kind that Tywin would doubtless enjoy – to

00:05:25.310 --> 00:05:28.949
know that Joffrey died by the same blade that
killed Ned Stark?

00:05:28.949 --> 00:05:35.400
The sword may NOT have caused a widow's wail
THIS time, but it certainly led a MOTHER to

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:36.400
mourn.

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:40.720
The Red Priestess is DEFINITELY dark and full
of terrors, but was it REALLY Miss Scarlett

00:05:40.720 --> 00:05:43.030
with the black magic in the dining room/bedroom?

00:05:43.030 --> 00:05:44.389
Let's look at the evidence.

00:05:44.389 --> 00:05:47.110
She's been involved in a death by poisoned
wine before.

00:05:47.110 --> 00:05:49.960
Remember Maester Cressen in season 2 who tried
to poison Melisandre?

00:05:49.960 --> 00:05:53.669
Well, they both drank from the SAME cup of
poisoned wine, but Melisandre was fine while

00:05:53.669 --> 00:05:54.669
Cressen keeled over, blood pouring from his
nose.

00:05:54.669 --> 00:05:56.879
Now, where have I seen that lately?

00:05:56.879 --> 00:06:00.870
Then there's Melisandre's attempt to show
Stannis Baratheon the POWER of king's blood,

00:06:00.870 --> 00:06:03.759
using the blood of Gendry, Robert Baratheon's
BASTARD son.

00:06:03.759 --> 00:06:09.250
She had Stannis throw leeches fat with Gendry's
blood into a fire while naming three USURPERS

00:06:09.250 --> 00:06:10.379
he wanted DEAD.

00:06:10.379 --> 00:06:15.380
The men he named were Robb Stark, Balon Greyjoy,
and Joffrey Baratheon.

00:06:15.380 --> 00:06:17.770
Well, Robb and Joffrey are already dead.

00:06:17.770 --> 00:06:22.199
SO, is Stannis-sandre the dark force behind
Joffrey's earthly departure?

00:06:22.199 --> 00:06:24.009
Or was it just coincidence?

00:06:24.009 --> 00:06:27.360
I bet Balon Greyjoy hopes so!

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:32.160
Sansa CERTAINLY had MORE than enough reasons
to do away with the King.

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:36.509
He beheaded her father in front of her, DESPITE
agreeing to show him mercy, and later forced

00:06:36.509 --> 00:06:38.810
her to look at Ned's head on a spike.

00:06:38.810 --> 00:06:42.319
When she initially refused, he had one of
his men strike her.

00:06:42.319 --> 00:06:46.659
He threatened her with a crossbow in front
of the whole court, before ordering her to

00:06:46.659 --> 00:06:47.659
be beaten.

00:06:47.659 --> 00:06:52.270
And his lies about the incident with Arya
and butcher's boy Mycah led to Sansa's direwolf

00:06:52.270 --> 00:06:53.949
Lady being killed.

00:06:53.949 --> 00:06:59.659
Not to mention his persistent jibes at his
wedding about her dead family, and that disgusting

00:06:59.659 --> 00:07:01.852
display of Robb Stark's death in the War of
5 dwarf Kings.

00:07:01.852 --> 00:07:02.852
The list is endless!

00:07:02.852 --> 00:07:03.900
So, who'd blame Sansa for killing the King?

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:04.900
No one!

00:07:04.900 --> 00:07:06.650
And she certainly had the opportunity.

00:07:06.650 --> 00:07:11.050
Remember when Joffrey kicked his gold goblet
away from Tyrion to humiliate his new cupbearer,

00:07:11.050 --> 00:07:13.610
well, it went under Sansa's table.

00:07:13.610 --> 00:07:17.030
And it was Sansa who picked it up and handed
it back to Tyrion.

00:07:17.030 --> 00:07:21.169
Perhaps that gave her JUST enough time to
secrete something SINISTER in the goblet.

00:07:21.169 --> 00:07:25.310
AND there's the fact that people who flee
the scene of a crime tend to look a little

00:07:25.310 --> 00:07:26.310
bit guilty!

00:07:26.310 --> 00:07:29.980
But, she DOES seem a little surprised when
Dontos turns up to take her away and, let's

00:07:29.980 --> 00:07:35.690
face it, she hasn't exactly displayed the
same killer instinct as her sister Arya.

00:07:35.690 --> 00:07:41.490
Yes, he's got motive – remember Joffrey
was going to have him drowned in wine in season

00:07:41.490 --> 00:07:46.139
2, until Sansa and The Hound intervened, telling
the King it'd be bad luck to kill someone

00:07:46.139 --> 00:07:47.240
on his name day?

00:07:47.240 --> 00:07:51.340
And when Dontos performed at the wedding as
the King's fool, Joffrey egged on the crowd

00:07:51.340 --> 00:07:53.020
to pelt him with food.

00:07:53.020 --> 00:07:58.290
Plus, Dontos was there ready to whisk off
Sansa once the King hit the deck, telling

00:07:58.290 --> 00:08:00.969
her that if she wanted to live, she had to
leave.

00:08:00.969 --> 00:08:06.060
And THEN there's the small matter of the NECKLACE
Dontos gave Sansa in episode 1 of season 4

00:08:06.060 --> 00:08:09.099
why was he QUITE so insistent she take it?

00:08:09.099 --> 00:08:11.330
Do YOU believe that family heirloom story?

00:08:11.330 --> 00:08:15.719
He WAS at the wedding festivities too, so
maybe he could have interfered with the feast.

00:08:15.719 --> 00:08:18.949
After all, he DOES know his way round a barrel
of wine.

00:08:18.949 --> 00:08:22.861
But surely, Dontos is too much of a drunken
fool to orchestrate the death of the King

00:08:22.861 --> 00:08:24.879
by himself, right?

00:08:24.879 --> 00:08:31.310
Ah, Petyr Baelish, one of the most dangerous
and least trustworthy men in Westeros.

00:08:31.310 --> 00:08:33.680
A man whose influence is felt EVERYWHERE.

00:08:33.680 --> 00:08:38.780
And YET, he's been conspicuous by his ABSENCE
in episodes 1 and 2 of season 4.

00:08:38.780 --> 00:08:42.769
Ok, so his ship is SUPPOSED to have left for
the Vale of AIR-RIN at the end of season 3.

00:08:42.769 --> 00:08:47.260
But, just because he doesn't SEEM to be around,
doesn't mean events are beyond his control.

00:08:47.260 --> 00:08:50.120
After all, like Varys, he has his spies.

00:08:50.120 --> 00:08:55.250
For example, male prostitute Olyvar, who,
after sleeping with Loras in season 3, and

00:08:55.250 --> 00:08:58.410
found out about the Tyrells' plan to marry
Loras to Sansa.

00:08:58.410 --> 00:09:02.970
And THIS season, Olyvar's been keeping Oberyn
MARTELL entertained, and Littlefinger informed

00:09:02.970 --> 00:09:04.120
too no doubt.

00:09:04.120 --> 00:09:06.980
SO, did Littlefinger have a HAND in Joffrey's
death?

00:09:06.980 --> 00:09:11.350
Well, he's certainly DEVIOUS enough to do
so, and he's given himself a GREAT alibi by

00:09:11.350 --> 00:09:12.700
NOT attending the wedding.

00:09:12.700 --> 00:09:16.149
It wouldn't be the FIRST time he's tried to
frame Tyrion Lannister either.

00:09:16.149 --> 00:09:22.410
Who was it, after all, who told Catelyn Stark
that the dagger used in Bran's attempted assassination

00:09:22.410 --> 00:09:27.230
ACTUALLY belonged to Tyrion and that Tyrion
had won it from Littlefinger in a bet?

00:09:27.230 --> 00:09:28.230
EXACTLY!

00:09:28.230 --> 00:09:29.790
But WHY would he slay the sovereign?

00:09:29.790 --> 00:09:34.250
Think back to that conversation Littlefinger
and Varys had about the realm in season 3.

00:09:34.250 --> 00:09:38.550
You know the one where Littlefinger says that
‘Chaos is a ladder.

00:09:38.550 --> 00:09:40.560
Many who try to climb it fail.

00:09:40.560 --> 00:09:42.899
And some are given the chance to climb but
they refuse.

00:09:42.899 --> 00:09:46.940
They cling to the realm or the gods or love,
illusions.

00:09:46.940 --> 00:09:48.470
Only the ladder is real.

00:09:48.470 --> 00:09:50.769
The climb is all there is.'

00:09:50.769 --> 00:09:55.070
Obviously, Littlefinger is an aficionado of
chaos, and the more chaos the merrier.

00:09:55.070 --> 00:09:59.410
And a monarch meeting his maker is PRETTY
high up there when it comes to creating chaos.

00:09:59.410 --> 00:10:03.550
Chaos which would doubtless create MANY opportunities
for Littlefinger to climb higher and higher

00:10:03.550 --> 00:10:05.029
up that ladder.

00:10:05.029 --> 00:10:09.480
Just as the chaos of war allowed him to rise
to Lord of Harrenhal, after he arranged for

00:10:09.480 --> 00:10:12.750
the Tyrells to support the Lannisters at Blackwater
and beyond.

00:10:12.750 --> 00:10:16.339
SO, what would Littlefinger hope to gain SPECIFICALLY
from Joffrey's death?

00:10:16.339 --> 00:10:20.750
Well, if Dontos was whisking off Sansa to
Littlefinger, then Littlefinger would control

00:10:20.750 --> 00:10:25.790
what MOST characters believe to be the ONLY
remaining STARK KEY to the North.

00:10:25.790 --> 00:10:29.579
Which would mean more power to Littlefinger's
elbow – or should that be finger?

00:10:29.579 --> 00:10:30.579
Anyway

00:10:30.579 --> 00:10:33.010
He's already TRIED to take Sansa away before,
though she declined.

00:10:33.010 --> 00:10:37.940
Don't forget that Ros warned Shae and Varys
about Littlefinger having his eye on the eldest

00:10:37.940 --> 00:10:41.560
Stark daughter – and we all know how THAT
ended for Ros.

00:10:41.560 --> 00:10:46.110
THIS time though, Sansa had little choice
about leaving as it might not be long before

00:10:46.110 --> 00:10:49.440
the finger of suspicion was pointed at her
for Joffrey's death.

00:10:49.440 --> 00:10:53.740
And remember: Littlefinger was infatuated
with Sansa's mother Catelyn, but his love

00:10:53.740 --> 00:10:54.740
was unrequited.

00:10:54.740 --> 00:10:58.980
Wouldn't he therefore RELISH controlling Cat's
beautiful daughter Sansa, and it would give

00:10:58.980 --> 00:11:03.410
him a bit of revenge just like when he betrayed
Cat's husband Ned?

00:11:03.410 --> 00:11:04.830
SO, how did he do it?

00:11:04.830 --> 00:11:07.529
Well, where do you think drunken Dontos got
that necklace from?

00:11:07.529 --> 00:11:10.019
And WHY did he ACTUALLY give it to Sansa?

00:11:10.019 --> 00:11:13.519
Couldn't the REAL point of the necklace have
been to smuggle poison into the wedding without

00:11:13.519 --> 00:11:14.950
raising suspicion?

00:11:14.950 --> 00:11:18.050
And if the plan WERE discovered, Sansa would
make the perfect patsy.

00:11:18.050 --> 00:11:22.440
There's certainly seems to be NO limit to
what Littlefinger will do to get what he wants.

00:11:22.440 --> 00:11:27.660
As Varys told Olenna Tyrell, "he would see
this country burn if he could be king of the

00:11:27.660 --> 00:11:28.660
ashes".

00:11:28.660 --> 00:11:31.959
Oh boy, the more you think about it, the more
it seems that Petyr Baelish's fingerprints

00:11:31.959 --> 00:11:33.350
are ALL over this!

00:11:33.350 --> 00:11:37.170
But he would have needed someone RELIABLE
at the wedding to make sure the poison ended

00:11:37.170 --> 00:11:38.170
up in the right place

00:11:38.170 --> 00:11:42.611
NOW, did you notice that during the wedding
ceremony when the Septon says ‘cursed be

00:11:42.611 --> 00:11:49.079
he who would seek to tear them asunder', we
get a lovely shot FOCUSED on Olenna and Loras

00:11:49.079 --> 00:11:53.839
Tyrell, Oberyn Martell, and Pycelle behind
Margaery and Joffrey?

00:11:53.839 --> 00:11:55.290
Hmmm.

00:11:55.290 --> 00:11:56.750
Intriguing.

00:11:56.750 --> 00:11:59.329
And so to the Tyrell matriarch.

00:11:59.329 --> 00:12:02.399
We know Olenna's a woman of both wit and wealth.

00:12:02.399 --> 00:12:04.600
She isn't afraid to speak her mind.

00:12:04.600 --> 00:12:08.480
She's shrewd enough to be able to deal with
Tywin Lannister, and like him, she's a master

00:12:08.480 --> 00:12:10.290
of political power games.

00:12:10.290 --> 00:12:12.639
But why would she want to bump off her grandson-in-law?

00:12:12.639 --> 00:12:16.870
Well, she's obviously not impressed with Joffrey's
behaviour, to say the least

00:12:16.870 --> 00:12:20.899
Sansa called him a ‘monster' when Olenna
asked her what she thought of him.

00:12:20.899 --> 00:12:24.460
And did you SEE the look on Olenna's face
at the end of the dwarf entertainment?

00:12:24.460 --> 00:12:28.660
A smart cookie like Olenna could see that
Margaery would ONLY be able to control the

00:12:28.660 --> 00:12:29.660
King so far.

00:12:29.660 --> 00:12:34.220
With Joffrey GONE, Margaery would be set to
marry the much-more-malleable next-in-line

00:12:34.220 --> 00:12:35.750
to the Iron Throne, Tommen.

00:12:35.750 --> 00:12:40.530
Therefore Olenna could keep Margaery away
from Joffrey's crossbow while STILL joining

00:12:40.530 --> 00:12:43.690
the royal bloodline, which would help House
Tyrell grow strong.

00:12:43.690 --> 00:12:45.709
So, how did she do it?

00:12:45.709 --> 00:12:49.910
Well, Olenna was definitely fiddling with
something in her hands as she spoke to Tywin

00:12:49.910 --> 00:12:50.910
on the way to the feast.

00:12:50.910 --> 00:12:54.259
Could it have been a little something to add
to Joffrey's wine?

00:12:54.259 --> 00:12:57.270
But she's too clever to risk it being seen
like that, isn't she?

00:12:57.270 --> 00:13:01.779
She ALSO makes a point of touching Sansa's
hair and neck as she consoles her about her

00:13:01.779 --> 00:13:06.899
brother Robb's death, telling here that ‘War
is war, but killing a man at a wedding, horrid.

00:13:06.899 --> 00:13:09.339
What sort of MONSTER would do such a thing?'

00:13:09.339 --> 00:13:13.810
Olenna could have taken this opportunity to
pick up something previously planted on Sansa

00:13:13.810 --> 00:13:15.529
to do in Joffrey.

00:13:15.529 --> 00:13:19.720
Drunken fool Dontos DID insist Sansa take
his family necklace as a thank-you for saving

00:13:19.720 --> 00:13:23.079
his life, and she's CLEARLY wearing it at
the wedding.

00:13:23.079 --> 00:13:24.079
But what's this?

00:13:24.079 --> 00:13:28.170
Is that a stone missing from the necklace
after Olenna fussed over Sansa?

00:13:28.170 --> 00:13:29.310
I think it is!

00:13:29.310 --> 00:13:33.950
And what's that little CLINK we hear and that
little motion of the arm we see as Olenna

00:13:33.950 --> 00:13:35.880
walks past Margaery's table?

00:13:35.880 --> 00:13:40.769
Did she pass the poison stone from Sansa's
necklace on to Margaery, OR into Joffrey's

00:13:40.769 --> 00:13:41.769
goblet?

00:13:41.769 --> 00:13:43.850
So, Olenna could be in cahoots with Littlefinger.

00:13:43.850 --> 00:13:48.230
She'd certainly be a reliable person to have
on the ground and the Tyrells have much to

00:13:48.230 --> 00:13:49.230
gain.

00:13:49.230 --> 00:13:50.230
Olenna also suggests that Sansa should visit
Highgarden – just as Margaery did in season

00:13:50.230 --> 00:13:51.230
3 – perhaps to make sure she's out of harm's
way, not only from Littlefinger this time,

00:13:51.230 --> 00:13:52.230
but also from anyone who MIGHT think Sansa
was involved in a plot to murder her former

00:13:52.230 --> 00:13:53.230
fiancé.

00:13:53.230 --> 00:13:54.230
Or POSSIBLY to incriminate her OR her husband
Tyrion.

00:13:54.230 --> 00:13:55.230
When no one does anything to aid the choking
Joffrey, Olenna DOES order the wedding guests

00:13:55.230 --> 00:13:56.230
to help their king.

00:13:56.230 --> 00:13:57.230
Was this a genuine desire to help?

00:13:57.230 --> 00:13:58.850
Or a clever way to take suspicion from herself?

00:13:58.850 --> 00:14:03.400
If Olenna was behind the plot, all this would
come with a delicious side-serving of retaliation

00:14:03.400 --> 00:14:08.759
on Tywin for forcing Loras to marry Cersei,
which scuppered Olenna's plans to marry him

00:14:08.759 --> 00:14:12.870
to Sansa in season 3.

00:14:12.870 --> 00:14:16.110
Season 4 marks the first time we've seen Mace
Tyrell on screen.

00:14:16.110 --> 00:14:20.610
Lord of Highgarden and head of one of the
RICHEST families in Westeros, Mace was keen

00:14:20.610 --> 00:14:24.990
on increasing his family's prestige by wedding
his daughter Margaery to Joffrey.

00:14:24.990 --> 00:14:28.230
SURELY that means he WOULDN'T have knocked
off his new son-in-law then.

00:14:28.230 --> 00:14:32.560
Add to that the fact that, according to his
mother Olenna, he's a "ponderous oaf" who

00:14:32.560 --> 00:14:36.759
places food above fighting, and we seem to
be erasing him from the list of suspects.

00:14:36.759 --> 00:14:39.750
But hold on, his wedding gift to Joffrey was
a gold cup, right?

00:14:39.750 --> 00:14:44.100
YES, but it WASN'T the gold goblet Joff was
drinking from when he croaked.

00:14:44.100 --> 00:14:49.940
Still, when Mace gave Joff his wedding gift,
he DID say, "may you drink deep and live long."

00:14:49.940 --> 00:14:53.990
Well, Joffrey certainly drank deep – he
wasn't quite so good at the living long part

00:14:53.990 --> 00:14:54.990
though!

00:14:54.990 --> 00:14:59.500
So, was this just a case of the show foreshadowing
Joffrey's death, or was Mace in on the murderous

00:14:59.500 --> 00:15:00.500
plan?

00:15:00.500 --> 00:15:02.560
He WAS sat next to Joffrey during the wedding
gift presentations.

00:15:02.560 --> 00:15:05.980
Could he have poisoned the King then with
a slow-acting potion?

00:15:05.980 --> 00:15:11.079
Is it possible that "fathead" Mace has more
upstairs than Olenna gives him credit for?

00:15:11.079 --> 00:15:12.470
But what about a motive?

00:15:12.470 --> 00:15:16.870
Well, his motive would be the same as Olenna's,
that is, to protect Margaery while keeping

00:15:16.870 --> 00:15:18.370
the crown.

00:15:18.370 --> 00:15:19.839
Hmmmm...

00:15:19.839 --> 00:15:22.060
And now, the brother of the bride.

00:15:22.060 --> 00:15:26.860
Loras was possibly in earshot when Joffrey
called Renly a "deviant" at his wedding feast

00:15:26.860 --> 00:15:30.779
and told Brienne he'd knight the man who put
a sword through his dead father's brother.

00:15:30.779 --> 00:15:36.029
Add to that the butt-naked dwarf running about
as Renly in Joffrey's vile entertainment,

00:15:36.029 --> 00:15:40.300
which led to Loras leaving the wedding table
in disgust, AND the fact that Joffrey told

00:15:40.300 --> 00:15:45.089
Margaery in season 3 that he was considering
making homosexuality punishable by death,

00:15:45.089 --> 00:15:47.329
and brother Tyrell has some POSSIBLE motives.

00:15:47.329 --> 00:15:48.329
But Loras does make a bit of a habit of storming
off from weddings – remember Tyrion and

00:15:48.329 --> 00:15:49.329
Sansa's wedding where Olenna made a comment
on his impending marriage to Cersei?

00:15:49.329 --> 00:15:52.670
Also, if Loras DIDN'T do the deed himself,
but his family, say Margaery or Olenna did,

00:15:52.670 --> 00:15:55.129
do you think they'd have let Loras in on it?

00:15:55.129 --> 00:15:56.270
Probably not!

00:15:56.270 --> 00:16:01.000
After all, he gave the game away to Littlefinger's
spy and prostitute Olyvar about their plans

00:16:01.000 --> 00:16:04.540
to marry Loras off to Sansa, thus ruining
that Tyrell plot.

00:16:04.540 --> 00:16:09.550
So, Loras is probably OFF the list of suspects.

00:16:09.550 --> 00:16:14.861
Since we first met Oberyn Martell, aka The
Red Viper, in episode 1 of season 4, it's

00:16:14.861 --> 00:16:18.500
been PRETTY obvious that he's NOT EXACTLY
the Lannisters' biggest fan.

00:16:18.500 --> 00:16:22.420
Of course, he's NOT the ONLY one in the show
who could DEFINITELY live without hearing

00:16:22.420 --> 00:16:27.600
The Rains of Castamere, but he has harboured
a long-standing grudge against House Lannister

00:16:27.600 --> 00:16:31.009
for their part in the death of his sister
Elia and her kids.

00:16:31.009 --> 00:16:34.690
Remember that Elia – who was married to
Prince Rhaegar Targaryen – was raped and

00:16:34.690 --> 00:16:39.490
killed by Gregor Clegane, aka The Mountain,
when the Lannisters sacked King's Landing

00:16:39.490 --> 00:16:41.610
just before Robert Baratheon became king.

00:16:41.610 --> 00:16:42.610
So, Oberyn is not only a lover but ALSO a
fighter and one who appears pretty intent

00:16:42.610 --> 00:16:43.610
on toppling The Mountain for his crimes.

00:16:43.610 --> 00:16:44.610
But why kill Joffrey?

00:16:44.610 --> 00:16:45.610
Why not just knock off The Mountain?

00:16:45.610 --> 00:16:47.720
An eye for an eye maybe?

00:16:47.720 --> 00:16:50.120
Maybe the King's death is just the start!

00:16:50.120 --> 00:16:54.740
Oberyn blames Tywin and his family for the
deaths of Elia and her children, as he believes

00:16:54.740 --> 00:16:58.290
Gregor would NOT have acted without Tywin's
consent.

00:16:58.290 --> 00:17:02.680
And as Oberyn told Tyrion when they first
met, "the Lannisters aren't the only ones

00:17:02.680 --> 00:17:03.680
who pay their debts."

00:17:03.680 --> 00:17:04.680
I bet the Lannisters wouldn't want to be on
the receiving end of the Red Viper's VENONMOUS

00:17:04.680 --> 00:17:05.680
bite!

00:17:05.680 --> 00:17:08.510
Then there was that verbal sparring session
between Cersei, Tywin, Oberyn and his lover

00:17:08.510 --> 00:17:12.360
Ellaria Sand at the wedding, where they traded
mutual insults.

00:17:12.360 --> 00:17:17.169
That culminated in what COULD be viewed as
a veiled threat by Oberyn against Cersei's

00:17:17.169 --> 00:17:21.589
daughter Myrcella, who was shipped off to
Dorne in season 2 to be married to Oberyn's

00:17:21.589 --> 00:17:22.589
nephew:

00:17:22.589 --> 00:17:27.709
This is what Oberyn said to Cersei: "In some
places, the highborn frown upon those of low

00:17:27.709 --> 00:17:28.709
birth.

00:17:28.709 --> 00:17:32.470
In other places, the rape and murder of women
and children is considered distasteful.

00:17:32.470 --> 00:17:38.030
What a fortunate thing for you, former Queen
Regent, that your daughter Myrcella has been

00:17:38.030 --> 00:17:40.340
sent to live in the latter sort of place."

00:17:40.340 --> 00:17:41.340
Oooh!

00:17:41.340 --> 00:17:45.160
So, could he have been helped by Ellaria in
his plot to rid the realm of Joffrey?

00:17:45.160 --> 00:17:47.669
Yes, he's Joffrey's real father.

00:17:47.669 --> 00:17:52.960
But does that really matter in a world where
siblings sleep together, brother kills brother,

00:17:52.960 --> 00:17:54.390
and father scorns son?

00:17:54.390 --> 00:17:58.240
It's not like Joffrey wasn't known for getting
RIGHT under people's skin!

00:17:58.240 --> 00:18:03.140
Just look at how he taunted Jaime in episode
1 of season 4, saying that Jaime had never

00:18:03.140 --> 00:18:06.430
done anything worthy of being recorded in
the history book of the Kingsguard.

00:18:06.430 --> 00:18:11.340
And look how depressed Jaime is in episode
2 of season 4 about being unable to fight

00:18:11.340 --> 00:18:13.070
since losing his sword hand.

00:18:13.070 --> 00:18:15.850
But, come on, would Jaime really have offed
Joffrey?

00:18:15.850 --> 00:18:19.789
After all, he's actually the first one to
go to Joffrey's side when the young King falls

00:18:19.789 --> 00:18:20.870
to the ground.

00:18:20.870 --> 00:18:25.250
Fatherly instinct or just doing his job?

00:18:25.250 --> 00:18:29.929
His position as a MAESTER, a man of science
and medicine among other things, means he

00:18:29.929 --> 00:18:33.169
has access to all sorts of potions and poisons.

00:18:33.169 --> 00:18:36.990
And Cersei's needling of him at the wedding
festivities – telling him that his every

00:18:36.990 --> 00:18:40.780
breath annoys her – wouldn't EXACTLY have
put him in a GOOD mood.

00:18:40.780 --> 00:18:45.340
But then again, he WAS sent away from the
wedding by Cersei, who ordered him to tell

00:18:45.340 --> 00:18:48.740
the kitchens to give the leftovers from the
feast to the kennels.

00:18:48.740 --> 00:18:52.240
So, that means he was out of the way and therefore
couldn't have done it, right?

00:18:52.240 --> 00:18:57.470
Not exactly, as we DO later see Pycelle sitting
opposite Varys during the mock tournament.

00:18:57.470 --> 00:18:59.960
Could he have been involved then in the murderous
plot?

00:18:59.960 --> 00:19:05.409
Ok, we all know what a wily character Pycelle
is, pretending he's a bit deaf or a bit old

00:19:05.409 --> 00:19:09.800
and creaky, as the situation requires, and
then leaping to life when no one's around.

00:19:09.800 --> 00:19:15.820
But TYWIN'S on to his little game, and Pycelle
seems WAY too intent on keeping his head down,

00:19:15.820 --> 00:19:19.770
and toadying up to whoever's in power to risk
his neck killing the King.

00:19:19.770 --> 00:19:24.840
It's no wonder he's been a Grand Maester – the
King's personal maester – for so many years.

00:19:24.840 --> 00:19:28.650
Did you notice how uncomfortable Varys looked
during the wedding festivities?

00:19:28.650 --> 00:19:33.760
Most of the guests were clapping when Margaery
announced leftovers from the feast were going

00:19:33.760 --> 00:19:38.820
to the poor, when the dwarf entertainers arrived,
when dwarf Robb Stark was killed in front

00:19:38.820 --> 00:19:43.140
of Sansa, and when dwarf Joffrey humped Robb's
direwolf head.

00:19:43.140 --> 00:19:46.030
But Varys didn't join in; he just looked rather
on edge.

00:19:46.030 --> 00:19:51.140
Now, of course Joffrey's vile entertainment
would be enough to make anyone uneasy, but

00:19:51.140 --> 00:19:54.480
isn't Varys often better at hiding what he
thinks than that?

00:19:54.480 --> 00:19:58.230
Is it possible the Spider spun a wily web
to kill Joffrey?

00:19:58.230 --> 00:20:03.900
Judging by his refusal to lie to the Lannisters
about Shae, when Tyrion asks him to, it doesn't

00:20:03.900 --> 00:20:07.029
SEEM likely he'd have the balls to off Joff.

00:20:07.029 --> 00:20:12.630
So maybe his unease at the wedding was ACTUALLY
down to his knowledge that someone else had

00:20:12.630 --> 00:20:14.100
a plot in motion.

00:20:14.100 --> 00:20:16.870
After all, he DOES have his little birds.

00:20:16.870 --> 00:20:17.870
So, who done it?

00:20:17.870 --> 00:20:18.870
What do YOU think?

00:20:18.870 --> 00:20:19.870
Tell us in the comments below.

00:20:19.870 --> 00:20:20.870
And while you're at it, remember to like our
video and subscribe to Flicks And The City

00:20:20.870 --> 00:20:21.870
for TONS more Game of Thrones reviews and
interviews.

00:20:21.870 --> 00:20:23.730
Just before we leave you, let's remind ourselves
of the wise words of Dwight Schrute from The

00:20:23.730 --> 00:20:24.730
Office:

00:20:24.730 --> 00:20:27.510
‘It's NEVER the person you MOST suspect.

00:20:27.510 --> 00:20:32.000
It's also NEVER the person you LEAST suspect,
since anyone with HALF a brain would suspect

00:20:32.000 --> 00:20:33.050
them the MOST.

00:20:33.050 --> 00:20:35.429
Therefore, I know the killer to be

00:20:35.429 --> 00:20:37.620
the person I most MEDIUM suspect.'

00:20:37.620 --> 00:20:48.650
So, who do YOU most MEDIUM suspect?

00:20:48.650 --> 00:20:54.520
And remember, if you're not watching Jan G
on GoT, you know nothin'!

